description:
src/lib.rs:43-49 — JmapMetadataExt::with_metadata_session is infallible:

    pub trait JmapMetadataExt {
        /// Create a [`SessionClient`] bound to this client and session.
        ///
        /// All JMAP Metadata method calls are made through the returned
        /// [`SessionClient`].
        fn with_metadata_session(&self, session: jmap_base_client::Session)
            -> methods::SessionClient;
    }

But the returned SessionClient is unusable if the Session does not advertise the metadata capability (i.e. session.primary_account_id("urn:ietf:params:jmap:metadata") returns None). In that case, every subsequent method call returns

    Err(ClientError::InvalidSession(
        "no primary account for urn:ietf:params:jmap:metadata".into()))

at the moment of the first call — see session_parts() at src/methods/mod.rs:248-258, which every builder method calls before serialising args.

The deferred-validation pattern is invisible from the trait method's signature and doc-comment. A caller's mental model — "if with_metadata_session succeeds, the returned SessionClient is usable" — silently violates reality. Failure is moved from construction time to first-call time. This forces every caller to handle ClientError::InvalidSession on every method call site (or manually walk session.primaryAccounts before construction to validate by hand).

Two fix paths:

(a) Type-the-contract. Change with_metadata_session to return Result<SessionClient, ClientError>, validating the capability at construction. Breaking signature change at 0.1.0; workspace-canonical propagation required (extension-client family consistency); minor ergonomic cost of an extra ? at each construction site.

(b) Document-the-contract. Add an explicit "# Deferred validation" or "# Errors-on-first-call" section to the trait method doc-comment stating that with_metadata_session does NOT validate the session and that the first method call may return Err(InvalidSession) if the session does not advertise the metadata capability. Non-breaking; cheap. Matches the "documented unsafety" pattern.

Recommendation: (b) for 0.1.0 (cheap, documents the actual behaviour), (a) for a future workspace-canonical revision pass once the canonical-template propagation rule allows. wzq9.13 ratified the extension-trait SHAPE; this finding is about the contract SEMANTICS of one trait method, orthogonal to the shape decision.

Workspace-wide: same deferred-validation gap exists on every extension-client with_<ext>_session method, since session_parts is the shared validation point. Propagate from canonical.

Cross-ref: wzq9.13 (shape approval — non-conflicting; this is about semantics not shape), wzq9.16 (ClientError::InvalidArgument(String) — note that the InvalidSession case here uses the same string-typed error variant).
